Well done, mortal!  But now thou must face the final Test...

The stupid Wizard again.  A final feast on the minataur.  Then some
confused fun with the ?oGoldDetection.  Oh it's all the way on the
other side.  Fortunatly he has a bout a billion /oDigging.  Zap Zap
Zap!

Now the plane of air.  Oh #@$@#@ forgot to do levitation first.  He
puts the ring on and then has some more confused fun with the scroll.
And once it again it's all the way on the other side.  He takes the
time to swtich from water walkers to boots of levitation and replace
the ring with conflict.  Much better!

He makes it just over half way when an air elemental gets him. Poly it
into a
giant ant!  It shortly happens again.  This time poly it into a Green
Elf. Oh and a 3rd time and yet another green elf.

He makes it to the plane of fire.  Repeat initial plane steps.  This
time it is smack dab in the center!  yeah a short trip.  He rests and
regain Pw for the plane of water and then enters the portal.  But
before He can enter the portal that pesky Wizard appears.  I think
this is the first time I've ever had him appear  above the plain of
Earth.  Usually Fire is the plain I encounter an Archon or two, so I'm
much happier to see the Wizard instead.  Then there was an incident
with a salamander.

He ended up with less Pw than if he had just gone through the portal
first thing.  Oh well the plane of water.  Usual plane entry steps.
Not having an "oMagicalBreathing he opts to stay in the bubble and
have the portal come to him.

Man does it take forever.  Ok he's got levitation and an "oLS, so go
ahead and risk it.  He finds it quickly!

The 2nd most wonderful words in the game appear:

You arrive on the Astral Plane!
Here the High Temples of the aligned gods are located.
You sense alarm, hostility, and excitement in the air!
A voice booms: "Thy desire for conflict shall be fulfilled!"

He arrive in the lower left.  Death guards the center alter.  Our hero
opts for the left alter. He finally lights his oil lamp.  Pestilince
is invisible. Hmmm that's a new one on me as well.  No difference it
dies.

He make his way through the conflicted horde of A's and @'s.  Oh drat
it's a lwaful alter and he's neutral.  *Sigh* back through the hordes.
This time to the right alter (er well the alter on the right I should
say).

On the way he finds another oil lamp.  Ooops he's suddenly ill and
stunned.  I think it was that 5 next to him  I bet I know what it is.
Magic Missile takes care of it in one shot.

Famine guards the alter on the right.  He bursts through the door
before our hero can even open it.  Fortunatly the evil rider runs into
a magic missle and dies.  Our hero then gets swapmed by a horde of
ants and before he gets through the door Famine has returned.  Finger
of Death this time.

He finally makes it to the next door and take a little break to eat.
And Famine returns again!  However something kills the rider before
our hero can do antyhing.  Ya gotta love the =oConflict.
.

Our hero finally makes it to the alter on the right.  And guess what,
it isn't the right alter. :( Stupid chaotic alter.

So now our hero  must face Death. But first Famine is back.  Our hero
kill him and moves on.  Then he has a snack of a trapper corpse since
he's not saiated yet.  Famine returns and dies immediatly.

Our hero makes it to the center door.  An Angel of Moloch is kind
enough to kill Death for him. However he only make it half way to the
next door before Death returns.  Fortunatly magic misslies kill him.

Now finally our hero is at the right alter!


